cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Generic identifiability of no-skip multi-head attention transformers"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Henry"
    given-names: "Nathan W."
    affiliation: "Center for Human-Compatible AI, UC Berkeley"
    email: "nathan.henry@berkeley.edu"
date-released: 2026-07-13
repository-code: "https://github.com/nathanwhenry1/noskip_transformer_identifiability"
abstract: >-
  A deep causal multi-head softmax-attention transformer without skip connections is
  generically identifiable up to unique within-layer head permutations and a unique
  boundary-normalized chain of interface gauges under an explicit width condition.
  This repository contains a complete Lean 4 formalization against Mathlib v4.30.0,
  including an exact generic matrix-fiber theorem, freeness, and factor-level recovery.
keywords:
  - "softmax attention"
  - "multi-head attention"
  - "no-skip transformer"
  - "identifiability"
  - "generic fibers"
  - "Lean 4"
  - "formal verification"
